Article 5 The national guiding institution for local chronicles work shall make overall plans, organize coordination, and supervise and guide the local chronicles work nationwide.
The local chronicles work institution of the local people's government at or above the county level shall be in charge of the local chronicles work within its administrative region and perform the following duties:
(1) organizing, guiding, supervising and inspecting the local chronicles work;
(2) formulating work plans and compilation schemes for local chronicles;
(3) organizing the compilation of local chronicle books and local comprehensive yearbooks;
(4) collecting and preserving local chronicle documents and materials, organizing the collation of old chronicles, and promoting the study of chronicle theory;
(5) organizing the development and utilization of local chronicle resources.
